 "title": "Sulfur Metabolism in Yeast: Gene Expression and Chemical Interactions",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around the sulfur metabolism in yeast, specifically focusing on the genes HSU1 and MET17 and their interactions with various chemicals. HSU1 has multiple roles, including the production of sulfide and the expression of MET17, which is involved in sulfate metabolism. MET17 has a metabolic defect in budding yeast, and its deletion leads to inefficient sulfide assimilation. The cluster also includes various chemicals involved in sulfur metabolism, such as sulfate, sulfide, and hydrogen sulfide, which are sources of other chemicals like SMM and H2S. The relationships between these entities highlight the complex interactions between genes and chemicals in sulfur metabolism in yeast.",
